WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:04.600
Erika, would you like to come to the botanical gardens with me today?

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.620
You mean your grandma's botanical gardens? 

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.320
Yeah!

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:13.610
She said a really rare and beautiful rubellum lily has bloomed, and invited us over to see it. 

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.920
Okay then!

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.330
Now that it's settled, let's cut the chit-chat and go!

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.120
E-Erika! Wait just a second!

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.330
Peek-a-boo!

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.630
Hi! We're here, Tsubomi's grandma!

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.280
Welcome.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.930
Yuri!

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:37.950
{OP}

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.140
HeartCatch

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.600
Precure!

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.190
HeartCatch Precure!

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:49.150
Now, all together

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.660
HeartCatch Precure!

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.620
Let's make our flowers bloom

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:02.290
Within each of our chests,

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:04.960
they begin to sprout

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.620
The seeds of the heart

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:07.880
are growing

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:10.510
bit by bit

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.180
Red,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:11.800
white

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.090
and yellow

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.840
It's because these blooming buds are

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.260
all varied colors

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:18.720
that they

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.940
shine so brightly!

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:26.270
That smile that you've nurtured

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.770
with such care

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.480
will never wither

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.070
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.910
Now, all together

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.410
HeartCatch Precure!

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.080
Let's make our flowers bloom!

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.960
They're always right by our sides

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:48.800
So together

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.680
let's make those pretty flowers of our heart

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.630
bloom even more!

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.130
HeartCatch

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.590
Precure!

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.000
And here's something for you, Chypre and Coffret. {Took out the comma between 'Chypre' and 'and,' but depending on how she phrases the original JP (treats them as a pair or addresses them each individually), could also be 'you, Chypre, and you, Coffret...')}

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.730
Yay!

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:12.130
It's so sweet and delicious!

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.400
Still, what a coincidence this is.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.010
It's amazing you all just happened to show up on the same day.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.700
Grandma, you invited Yuri too, didn't you?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.370
Well, the plant's genus <i>is</i> otome-yuri after all.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.120
That's so funny!

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.120
Tsubomi!

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:36.280
Tsubomi, this is our opening!

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.240
Opening?

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.700
Yuri was Cure Moonlight, the Precure before us, right?

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.890
There's so many things I wanna ask her.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.370
Right, but...

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.610
I cannot fight alongside you.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.500
My mother is probably worried about me, so...

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:55.110
Yuri!

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.260
Just leave her alone for the moment, all right?

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.110
Grandma?

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:05.260
The damage that Sabark and Dark Precure inflicted on her heart has not yet healed.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.740
And since she lost her Seed of the Precure, Yuri...

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.170
can't become Cure Moonlight anymore.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.300
Oh, this won't do!

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.500
We're all out of tea cakes!

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.680
In that case, I'll go and buy some more.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.360
But you're a guest, Yuri! I'll go instead.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.020
Grandma, the usual shop's fine, right?

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:29.770
Fine by me.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.440
I'll come too!

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.520
It's fine, really.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.520
You two only just arrived, so please take it easy for a bit.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.280
I want to get some fresh air anyway.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.480
But...

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.900
Why don't you all go together then?

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:43.740
Okay!

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:44.870
We'll be off, then!

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.080
That's fine, right, Yuri?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:47.870
Sure.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.840
Please Recognize

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.840
Please Recognize

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.510
Yuri!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.110
What is it?

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.920
U-Um...

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.680
We were hoping you'd be able to give us some advice.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:16.500
Like how to fight better, or what the Desert Apostles' weaknesses are, or anything you think could help us! {Added the second 'or.'}

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.960
Please help us!

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:18.860
Please!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.490
I told you, didn't I?

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.780
I'm not going to concern myself dealing with you two.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.820
I'm not a Precure anymore.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.030
But...

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:33.830
Besides, the Desert Apostles are only going to become more fierce in their assaults.

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:39.250
If you're really seeking advice from me, then you might as well give up now.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.920
Moonlight!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:48.220
I've continued fighting all on my own, no matter how hard or how painful it gets!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.100
All so I could protect this world!

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.140
Do you really have that kind of resolve?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.260
I've never seen you put it on display.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:59.300
Cure Blossom, Cure Marine,

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.170
I don't recognize you as Precure.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.540
What the heck? She didn't have to be so rude.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.430
Right?

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.000
Yuri, this is the place!

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:14.770
Harano Confectionery.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.650
Their daifuku mochi are simply the best!

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.960
Their soy beans are boiled with just the right amount of salt,

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.840
and there's this subtle, refined sweetness to the bean paste. {Are you sure this is 'soya?'}

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.380
And it's all wrapped up in a smooth shell, like a rhapsodious trinity! {Sure is Lucky Star in here.}

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.940
It's enough to melt your heart.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:30.100
I wanna try one already!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.500
Show a little restraint!

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.310
Let's just buy some and head back, all right?

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.870
Good afternoon.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:38.900
Oh, it's Tsubomi!

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.500
Good afternoon, Chizuko!

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.600
We'd like our usual daifuku, please.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.650
Coming right up!

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.990
Like I said, what's the difference?

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.430
Oh, what's with you, Bro?

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.330
Tsubomi, can you just hold on a second?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.460
O-Okay.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:02.030
We've got customers. Keep it down!

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:03.970
Just answer me, Dad!

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:08.920
What's the difference between your daifuku and mine?! {Removed the 'just' at the start of this sentence, since I don't like two lines starting with the same word, and it flows better to take it out of this one.}

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:13.600
Have you tried so many of your own that 
you've forgotten how they're meant to taste?! {Changed the typoed 'to' to 'so.'}

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:21.980
Bro...

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:25.090
Chizuko, you mustn't keep our customers waiting.

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:25.780
Right!

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.580
I'm terribly sorry. You shouldn't've had to see that.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:30.570
It's fine.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.870
Is something the matter with Masahiro?

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:41.250
He's been training for a while, and they finally
 said he could start making the Harano daifuku,

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.500
but it looks like it's not going as well as he'd hoped.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.670
Harano Confectionery

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.670
Thanks for stopping by, anyway!

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.400
Well then, Cure Flower will be waiting for us!

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:53.290
Hey! Hold on a second!

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.410
Tsubomi, I'm sorry about just now.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:01.560
Um... the thing is, I have a favor to ask.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.650
What is it?

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:05.700
Could you ask your grandma to try these, Tsubomi?

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.820
Oh, thanks very much!

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:08.940
What are these?

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:10.990
The daifuku I made.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:14.410
I want to get some feedback from our regular customers.

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.020
They're delicious!{imokaywiththis.jpg}

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:21.640
Jeez, Erika!

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:27.380
It'd be nice if everyone was as easy to please as you.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.400
My old man and gramps are always so tough on me.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:34.400
They never tell me my stuff's tasty or give me a single word of praise.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.810
Really?

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:39.340
I'm third in line, so I'm gonna end 
up inheriting the shop eventually.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:43.700
I wanna make great daifuku so they'll recognize me as a deserving heir!

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:46.020
So I'm counting on you, Tsubomi!

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:54.120
And these are the Harano daifuku he made for you.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.740
I can't believe little Masa's all grown up and started making his own daifuku. {she uses "Ma-kun" rather than "Masa" but I think the honorific here would seem kinda weird and out of place. Up to you, fix if you prefer it.}

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.020
Time really does fly, doesn't it?

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:01.930
Let's see here.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.340
H-How are they?

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:13.300
They're nice, but he still has a ways to go.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:14.760
That's all you have to say?

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:15.930
I think so.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.500
That's harsh, Grandma.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:19.280
Right?

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:20.010
Right.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:33.720
I suppose Yuri thinks we still have a ways to go too, huh?

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.800
This is really irritating!

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.910
I want Yuri to recognize how much effort we put into this!

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.330
How do we do that?

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:47.840
Well, we just gotta beat the stuffing out of the Desert Apostles and make ourselves look really cool!

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.420
Come get some, Desert Apostles!

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.830
Don't tempt fate!

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:52.340
Ow...

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.010
Achoo!

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.760
I guess someone's talking about us.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:00.760
Hmph!

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:04.660
It has to be my fans revering my beauty.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.270
What are you talking about?

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:11.280
This sneezing was caused by manly spirits 
crying out in admiration of my magnificence!

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:12.570
It was because of me!

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:13.940
It was me!

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:16.540
No, it was me!

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.480
It was <i>me</i>!

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:17.990
Hmph!

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.580
I'm not gonna sink to your level.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:24.090
After all, if someone's calling for us, it'd be rude to keep them waiting!

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.900
What's the matter, Tsubomi?

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.400
Yuri...

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.570
Come in.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.210
Oh, Tsubomi. What's the matter?

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.040
There's something I wanted to ask you.

00:10:05.740 --> 00:10:11.720
Grandma, you used to fight the Desert Apostles as Cure Flower, didn't you?

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:12.500
Yes.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.710
Why exactly have the Desert Apostles appeared again?

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:23.110
The fact is, throughout history this world has been attacked by the Desert Apostles many times.

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:26.890
And every time, a Precure has arisen to defend it.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:32.110
I was chosen as a Precure when I was researching the Great Heart Tree,

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:35.360
and I was somehow able to drive the Desert Apostles away.

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:40.570
Then time passed, and the next Precure who 
would defend the Great Heart Tree was chosen.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.540
That was... Cure Moonlight.

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:46.730
She was truly powerful.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:51.290
I was certain we'd be able to defeat the Desert Apostles for good.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:52.630
But then...

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:54.570
Cure Moonlight was...

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.420
Yuri was defeated by Dark Precure.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:03.720
When I was Cure Flower, they didn't
 have such might amongst their ranks.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:07.230
A Dark Precure created for the purpose of defeating Precure...

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.920
And the one who created her, Sabark.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.610
We have to defeat them, no matter what.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:22.410
Grandma, Yuri told Erika and me that she doesn't recognize us as Precure.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.160
I see...

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:27.790
Will she recognize us if we become stronger?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:28.790
Perhaps so.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:34.170
If you became stronger as Precure, 
then Yuri might have to eat her words.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:41.430
But is becoming stronger really what's important here?

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:45.640
You should think about what's really important to you.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.100
What's really important to us...

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:06.150
All right!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.790
Harano Confectionery

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:11.260
You're really gonna do it, Tsubomi?

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:12.750
I promised him I would!

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:16.080
I've gotta give him Grandma's verdict.

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:18.460
You're just gonna hurt his feelings.

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.460
Yeah, I know...

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:23.150
But he won't understand unless you tell him.

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:23.930
You're right!

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:25.800
Good afternoon!

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:28.680
I'm terribly sorry, but my brother's kind of busy at the moment.

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:36.520
This is no good. Start over!

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:38.690
Why?

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.240
Why, Dad?!

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.840
Just tell me what's wrong with them already!

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:47.450
I cooked the beans just as long and I put in exactly the same amount of sugar!

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:50.210
I did everything the same way you did!

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:51.910
It should taste exactly the same!

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:57.300
Even with the same ingredients, changes in weather, temperature, and humidity

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.880
can all make slight changes in the flavor.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:04.930
If you'd just told me that beforehand, I could've done a better job.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:08.470
An artisan learns from experience, not by being told everything!

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.020
B-Bro!

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.180
Leave him, Chizuko.

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:17.830
We'll go after him!

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:18.940
Let's go, Tsubomi!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:20.900
Fishie-wishies! {kid is trying to say 'sakana' meaning fish but ends up saying 'chakana' because lol kid lisp. I figure this is a good way of conveying. Also, SONOZAKI SAKANA}

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:30.330
I worked so hard to get my old man and gramps to recognize me...

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:35.650
I've found a sad little man!

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:43.140
Flower of the Heart, come forth!

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:55.490
It's your cue, Desertrian!

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.580
Spa! Tula! Spa! Tula!

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:16.800
Th-That's...

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.960
Spatula!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.170
Take a look in the crystal!

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:23.250
Masahiro Flower of the Heart is the one that was stolen!

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.400
No way!

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:25.900
Erika, let's go!

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:26.800
Let's do it!

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:40.480
Go, Seeds of the Precure!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:44.950
Precure!

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.490
Open My Heart!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.140
A lone flower, blooming from the earth!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.450
Cure Blossom!

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:45.010
A lone flower, swaying in the sea breeze!

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.550
Cure Marine!

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:56.950
HeartCatch Precure!

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:05.520
Noooooooo!

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:06.820
Spatulalala!

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:14.020
Sasorina!

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:17.080
We're gonna take back the Flower of Masahiro's Heart!

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.540
Just 'cause you've gotten stronger lately doesn't mean you can be so cocky!

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.500
Go get 'em, Snackies!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:35.050
Marine Dynamite!

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:41.730
Tch.

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:44.350
Desertrian, smash them!

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.360
What's wrong with them?!

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.120
Stop playing with your food!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.250
Now just hold on a sec!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:02.700
Spatula!

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:11.570
That's it! Go wild! Let the petals from the Flower of your Heart fall away!

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:15.000
Spatula!

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:20.930
I have to become a worthy third in line!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:25.790
Why can't my old man and gramps just recognize how hard I'm trying!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.070
You're looking at this all wrong!

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:34.270
What's really important isn't to be recognized by others!

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.070
Spatula!

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:39.570
Masahiro! {lol -oniisan}

